// Purging a database is Rule 79's own example of the operation confirmation is
// RESERVED for, precisely because nothing can take it back.
//
// Offering UNDO here is worse than offering none: the operator acts believing
// there is a way back, and finds out there is not at the only moment it
// matters. The promise and the right contradict each other.
//
// Expected: IRREVERSIBLE_CLAIMS_UNDO

DEFINE INTERACTION purge_archive (
  SATISFIES [ACT, CONFIRM],
  ALWAYS_REACHABLE [UNDO, CANCEL],
  ROLE irreversible,
  ACTOR administrator
)
